    "edit_note": "An elevated hub's side structure (hand L, lift), origin on the LANE centre at bed level. The roof slab starts at the rail deck's edge (5.0 m) and carries the platform; nothing may come nearer the track than the platform edge (3.55 m) below 4.2 m (the gauge). At F1 the rail wall's line is the paid box's long side: a column at the module's +X end under a beam at the ceiling (3.8 m over the street)."
